{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1795214916291410002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"golden-busied-nag","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"fb21c059b6966a45b7cb6a67f3ab298814461010873d7bcd0ba2849bef3a0d54","event_uuid":"b2e35a1f-25da-41a6-bc85-79c3c3b216c8","position":{"commit_sha":"aeef790b957d7a76c3ac913a5c1832bec2e2c0a7","position":"1795213805057892001-b2e35a1f-25da-41a6-bc85-79c3c3b216c8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"630b49169afc5e6d27a183e9b1462946f24c83cfeda8307e1d9f9039eabd6331","event_uuid":"ddce8ef7-cb0a-4170-b233-0eef90f288f5","position":{"commit_sha":"a71aea08b682e145a86e43d4f9ae8223c92314f2","position":"1795213867988370001-ddce8ef7-cb0a-4170-b233-0eef90f288f5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"0e0100da8b3e66a34a9c99e6cd469cf4a2dcb8c1c7e2bca876b91296f44ee190","event_uuid":"152c83c4-aced-42ee-90eb-38f48ee32f7b","position":{"commit_sha":"3aeb8abe9ae3bfe2df0082fbd28f225363bed5da","position":"1795214879343949001-152c83c4-aced-42ee-90eb-38f48ee32f7b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"fab910daef35053cb6091addc33aba07f059406e5f336c1cc3f99b4795d00204","event_uuid":"8854f0fa-d05e-4cdb-9b8d-1c791bb2b5ee","position":{"commit_sha":"55fefe99b425259c56748267dc785a95ab0c0b7c","position":"1795214916291410001-8854f0fa-d05e-4cdb-9b8d-1c791bb2b5ee"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision, 2026-11-20: the simple solution is that CI checks op-cert trust using main's rebar.toml, not the rebar.toml in the change under review. A change can then never widen the trust list of the gate that checks it.","timestamp":1795214879343949001}],"created_at":1795213805057892001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ddce8ef7-cb0a-4170-b233-0eef90f288f5","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from nonblack-brigandish-guillemot: its closing plan review raised this as an advisory finding. After ADR 0125, rebar checks op-certs for validity only unless the verifying environment lists the keys it trusts in `verify.trusted_opcert_keys`. ADR 0125 says that list belongs to each environment's own configuration, not the repository.\n\nNothing enforces that. `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` is an ordinary `[verify]` key (`src/rebar/_config_sections.py:83`). No code restricts which config layer may set it; a search of `src/rebar/_config*.py` finds no repository-scope restriction for any key. The op-cert gate resolves its configuration through the repository root, so a committed `rebar.toml` that sets the key is read like any other layer. A change under review could add a key to that file and widen the trust list of the very gate that checks it.\n\n## Approach (operator decision, 2026-11-20)\n\nCI resolves the op-cert gate's trust configuration from main's `rebar.toml`, never from the `rebar.toml` in the change under review. A change can then edit `rebar.toml` freely, but its edit only takes effect for gating after it has itself merged through review.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The CI op-cert gate reads `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` from main's `rebar.toml`, not the change's.\n- [ ] A change that adds a key to `rebar.toml` does not widen the trust list its own gate run uses, shown by a test that tries it.\n- [ ] No config key, env var or flag is added by the fix.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"eca7-e5b5-7640-403f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"A committed rebar.toml can widen the op-cert gate's trust list","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b2e35a1f-25da-41a6-bc85-79c3c3b216c8","ddce8ef7-cb0a-4170-b233-0eef90f288f5","152c83c4-aced-42ee-90eb-38f48ee32f7b","8854f0fa-d05e-4cdb-9b8d-1c791bb2b5ee"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795214916291410002,"uuid":"c85f24a7-38e2-483f-8830-48d5c1044f84"}